    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1042">

                <pb facs="0780" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg664"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 125.8273/62b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul General Hanna.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 19, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department is considering advisability of requesting Huerta to issue orders to
                    his federal commander at Saltillo to the end that Silliman and any Americans
                    with him may be released and escorted by a federal escort, under a flag of
                    truce, toward Monterey until the Constitutionalist lines shall have been
                    reached; and desires to know, if Huerta consents to issuance of such orders,
                    whether Constitutionalist commander in authority at Monterey will send out a
                    guard, under a flag of truce, to receive Silliman and party and convey them
                    safety to Monterey.</p>
                <p>If Constitutionalist authority at Monterey is inclined to receive this suggestion
                    favorably, you will kindly telegraph Department with least possible delay,
                    describing accurately the point to which the Constitutionalist authority will be
                    willing to send its guard, so that with this knowledge in its possession
                    Department may make proper representations to General Huerta.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
